  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nInitial ratio = 2 : 3 : 4\n\nIncrease = 50%, 40%, 30%\n\n**Formula Used:**\n\nNew value = Original × (1 + increase/100)\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n⇒ 2 × 100 = 200\n\n⇒ 3 × 100 = 300\n\n⇒ 4 × 100 = 400\n\n⇒ 200 × 150 ÷ 100 = 300\n\n⇒ 300 × 140 ÷ 100 = 420\n\n⇒ 400 × 130 ÷ 100 = 520\n\n⇒ Ratio = 300 : 420 : 520\n\n⇒ Divide by 20\n\n⇒ Ratio = 15 : 21 : 26\n\n**∴ The correct answer is 15 : 21 : 26.**",
